# The Times and the staged events (Docs/Design/79-a-staged-economy.md, sections 5.3, 8.4, 8.5 and 11; Phase 8): how each
# band and class speaks of hard and good times and their cause, and of the week's happenings at the market.
#
# talk.times: world.times (hard, lean, ordinary, good, boom) and world.times_cause (a noun phrase, maybe missing: the
# slider's cause, a harvest, the robbed wagons, an event's words, the DM's own; said after "talk of", "word of", "blames"
# or alone). Openers remember what kind of thing was said, two minutes, so every reply fits what it answers:
#   tm=moan   times are hard on me (or good times that haven't reached me)
#   tm=cause  why, in the cause's words
#   tm=state  a rich upper-class wolf on the Houses, the Council, the Crown (class-gated: never a carter's talk)
#   tm=land   a rich wolf of the middle or lower class, or of the towns: land, mills, the harvest, their own trade
#   tm=boast  times are good to me
# then times.answer (moan, cause, and the rich's worries in hard times), times.boast_answer (a boast, the rich's talk in
# good times), and times.close after a sour answer (ta=sour).
#
# talk.event: world.event (the kind's id), world.event_words (a noun phrase), world.event_when (now, soon, past). Never
# a price figure, and a good is said to be dear or cheap only where its world.<good>_price says so (the list shows it);
# an event over is spoken of in the past. Openers remember ev=bad, ev=good, ev=loss or ev=news for event.answer.

## ================================================================ The Times: hard and lean, by band and class

rule e8t_hard_destitute
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=destitute
cooldown 1d
say Times like these, it's #dole# or nothing. | Nobody gives a penny when everyone's #skint#.
remember pair: tm=moan 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_hard_poor
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=poor self.class=lower|middle
cooldown 1d
say What I earn doesn't stretch to Emberday any more. | They've cut the hours at my place. Same work, less of it, less pay.
remember pair: tm=moan 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_hard_poor_upper
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=poor self.class=upper
cooldown 2d
say One sold the good silver last month. Not a word to anyone. | We keep up appearances. Appearances are cheaper than dinners.
remember pair: tm=moan 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_hard_comfortable
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=comfortable
cooldown 1d
say We're tightening our belts. Another notch and I'll be through it. | Folk are buying less. You feel it at every counter.
remember pair: tm=moan 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_hard_rich_state
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=rich self.class=upper here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say The Council will have to answer for this. In the chamber, not the street. | The Houses will be asked to stand behind the Crown. They always are.
remember pair: tm=state 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_hard_rich_father
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=rich self.class=upper self.father
cooldown 2d
say Father says the Houses must close ranks until it passes. | Father has the steward looking at every account twice.
remember pair: tm=state 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_hard_rich_house
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=rich self.house
cooldown 2d
say Our House will see its people through. It always has. | Our House has put off the summer ball. Imagine the talk.
remember pair: tm=state 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_hard_rich_land
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=rich self.class=middle|lower
cooldown 1d
say The mill's turning half days. Nobody's buying flour by the sack. | My tenants are behind with the rent. I can't turn them all out.
remember pair: tm=land 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_hard_rich_town
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=rich here.region!=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say The fields don't care about the times. The market does. | I'll hold my grain back till it turns. Let the barns wait.
remember pair: tm=land 2m
then other: times.answer

## The cause, in its own words

rule e8t_cause_hard
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean world.times_cause
cooldown 1d
say It's all the talk of #world.times_cause#, they say. | Ever since word of #world.times_cause#, nothing's been right. | Everyone blames #world.times_cause#. I suppose they're right.
remember pair: tm=cause 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_cause_hard_poor
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean world.times_cause self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say #world.times_cause.capitalize#. And who pays for it? Us, same as ever. | They talk of #world.times_cause#. I talk of my supper.
remember pair: tm=cause 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_cause_hard_upper
when concept=talk.times world.times=hard|lean world.times_cause self.wealth=rich|comfortable self.class=upper here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say The Heights talk of nothing but #world.times_cause#. | #world.times_cause.capitalize#. A matter of state, and the city pays for it.
remember pair: tm=cause 2m
then other: times.answer

## Good times and boom

rule e8t_good_destitute
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom self.wealth=destitute
cooldown 1d
say Good times, they say. Not on the chapel steps. | Boom for some. I'm still counting crumbs.
remember pair: tm=moan 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_good_poor
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom self.wealth=poor
cooldown 1d
say Good times, they say. Not on my street. | The #toffs# are spending. Spending past me.
remember pair: tm=moan 2m
then other: times.answer

rule e8t_good_comfortable
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom self.wealth=comfortable
cooldown 1d
say Good times. We had meat twice this week. | Work's steady and the pay keeps coming. I'll take it.
remember pair: tm=boast 2m
then other: times.boast_answer

rule e8t_good_comfortable_parent
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom self.wealth=comfortable self.parent=yes
cooldown 2d
say The pups have new boots, and I didn't have to think about it. | The little ones had a cake on Restday. A whole cake.
remember pair: tm=boast 2m
then other: times.boast_answer

rule e8t_good_comfortable_keeper
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom self.wealth=comfortable self.role=merchant business=thriving|steady
cooldown 1d
say A queue at my counter yesterday. A queue! | I've taken on a lad to help. First time in years.
remember pair: tm=boast 2m
then other: times.boast_answer

rule e8t_good_rich_state
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom self.wealth=rich self.class=upper here.region=ridgemere
cooldown 1d
say The Houses haven't had a season like it. The Council's all smiles. | The Crown's pleased with the city, one hears. That's worth more than coin.
remember pair: tm=state 2m
then other: times.boast_answer

rule e8t_good_rich_cheese
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom self.wealth=rich
cooldown 2d
say We've a whole wheel of the good cheese in the larder. A whole wheel. | Cheese at every supper this week. One gets used to it terribly fast.
remember pair: tm=boast 2m
then other: times.boast_answer

rule e8t_good_rich_land
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom self.wealth=rich self.class=middle|lower
cooldown 1d
say Mill's never been busier. I've bought the meadow by the river. | My barns are full and my buyers are fuller. Good years, these.
remember pair: tm=land 2m
then other: times.boast_answer

rule e8t_cause_good
when concept=talk.times world.times=good|boom world.times_cause
cooldown 1d
say #world.times_cause.capitalize#, and suddenly everyone's got coin. | All this talk of #world.times_cause#, and the whole city's different.
remember pair: tm=cause 2m
then other: times.answer

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Answers: a moan or a cause, in hard times

rule e8t_ans_hard_destitute
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan|cause world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=destitute
say Try the chapel steps. Then tell me about hard. | At least you've a roof.

rule e8t_ans_hard_poor
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan|cause world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=poor
say Don't I know it. I'm #skint# till Marketday. | Same here. Every penny's counted twice.

rule e8t_ans_hard_poor_parent
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan|cause world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=poor self.parent=yes
say #agree#. My pups are eating porridge for supper. | And the little ones growing out of everything.

rule e8t_ans_hard_comfortable
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan|cause world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=comfortable
say We're all pinching. #agree#. | Keep your head down and your purse shut, that's my way.

rule e8t_ans_hard_rich_upper
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan|cause world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=rich self.class=upper
say It is being seen to, I'm told. At the Council. | Dreadful. Someone really ought to do something.

rule e8t_ans_hard_rich
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan|cause world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=rich self.class=middle|lower
say I've cut my hands to four days. It's that or shut the gate. | It'll pass. Buy cheap now, I say.

rule e8t_ans_hard_any
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan|cause world.times=hard|lean
say #agree#. It'll turn. It always does. | #oath#. I don't know anyone who isn't feeling it.

## The rich's worries, answered

rule e8t_ans_worry_poor
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=state|land world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Your half days are my no days. | I'd trade worries with you. Gladly.
remember pair: ta=sour 2m
then other: times.close

rule e8t_ans_worry_any
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=state|land world.times=hard|lean
say So I hear. | Hard for everyone, then. | Quite. One rides it out.

## A moan in good times (the poor not feeling it), and a cause in good or ordinary times

rule e8t_ans_good_moan_rich
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan world.times=good|boom self.wealth=rich
say Nonsense. There's work for anyone who wants it. | It'll trickle down. It always does, eventually.
remember pair: ta=sour 2m
then other: times.close

rule e8t_ans_good_moan_poor
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=moan world.times=good|boom self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Not my street either. | Good times never get down the hill.

rule e8t_ans_cause_good
when concept=times.answer pair.mem.tm=cause world.times=good|boom
say Long may it last. | I'll believe it when it's in my purse.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Answers to a boast, and the close

rule e8t_boast_ans_poor
when concept=times.boast_answer self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Must be nice. | Good for you. Some of us are still counting crusts.
remember pair: ta=sour 2m
then other: times.close

rule e8t_boast_ans_comfortable
when concept=times.boast_answer self.wealth=comfortable
say Good for you. Mind it doesn't turn. | Make hay while the sun shines, eh?

rule e8t_boast_ans_rich
when concept=times.boast_answer self.wealth=rich
say We've done well too, touch wood. | Yes, everyone's flush. It makes servants so hard to keep.

rule e8t_boast_ans_any
when concept=times.boast_answer
say Well, that's good to hear. | Glad someone's doing well.

rule e8t_close_any
when concept=times.close pair.mem.ta=sour
say I didn't mean anything by it. | Fair enough. | Sorry. I didn't think.

## ================================================================ Barks: hard and lean times

rule e8t_bk_hard_destitute
when concept=bark world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=destitute
cooldown 4h
say A penny, anyone? Times are hard for all of us. | Hard times. Hard ground to sleep on.

rule e8t_bk_hard_poor
when concept=bark world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=poor
cooldown 4h
say Another week, another hole in the purse. | #oath#, these times.

## ================================================================ The week's events
## (Each: what it is while on and coming; what was, once it's over; a good dear or cheap only by its price fact.)

## A House wedding (the city's).

rule e8t_ev_wedding_soon
when concept=talk.event world.event=house_wedding world.event_when=soon
cooldown 1d
say There's a House wedding on the way. Every cook in the Heights is hiring. | A House wedding this week. The whole city will turn out to gawp.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_wedding_now
when concept=talk.event world.event=house_wedding world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say Carriages up and down the hill all day. For the wedding. | They've hung ribbons from every lamp on the way up to the Heights.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_wedding_wine
when concept=talk.event world.event=house_wedding world.event_when=soon|now world.wine_price=up
cooldown 1d
say The stewards are buying up all the wine for the wedding. Dear as anything. | Wine's dear while the Houses buy for the wedding.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_wedding_mother
when concept=talk.event world.event=house_wedding world.event_when=soon|now self.wealth=rich self.class=upper self.mother
cooldown 1d
say We're invited, of course. Mother has had three gowns made and likes none of them. | The seating alone has caused two feuds.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_wedding_poor
when concept=talk.event world.event=house_wedding world.event_when=soon|now self.wealth=poor|destitute
cooldown 1d
say A House wedding. They'll spend more on one night than I'll see in my life. | Maybe they'll throw the leftovers to the gate.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_wedding_cook
when concept=talk.event world.event=house_wedding world.event_when=soon|now self.job=cook|baker|brewer|innkeeper
cooldown 1d
say Every kitchen in the city's working for the House wedding. | The stewards want it all by morning. All of it.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_wedding_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=house_wedding world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say Did you see the House wedding? The carriages! | They're still sweeping ribbons off the hill, after the wedding.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

## A fire at the works.

rule e8t_ev_fire_now
when concept=talk.event world.event=works_fire world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say There's a fire at the works. You can see the smoke from the square. | They're saying the works caught fire in the night.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_fire_worker
when concept=talk.event world.event=works_fire world.event_when=now self.quarter=works
cooldown 1d
say I was there when it went up. The heat took the fur off my arm. | We passed buckets till dawn. It's still smouldering.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_fire_builder
when concept=talk.event world.event=works_fire world.event_when=now self.job=crafter|laborer
cooldown 1d
say I can't get planks for love nor money since the fire. | Anyone building had better wait till the works is put right.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_fire_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=works_fire world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say They're still clearing the burnt beams at the works. | Nobody hurt in the fire, thank the Bright One.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

## A good catch.

rule e8t_ev_catch_now
when concept=talk.event world.event=good_catch world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say The boats came in low in the water this morning. | A good catch in. Everyone's having fish tonight.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_catch_cheap
when concept=talk.event world.event=good_catch world.event_when=now world.fish_price=down
cooldown 1d
say A good catch is in. Fish is cheap for a day or two. | Fish going for nothing at the stalls, with the catch in.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_catch_fisher
when concept=talk.event world.event=good_catch world.event_when=now self.job=fisher|sailor
cooldown 1d
say Best haul of the season. The nets near split. | We'll be salting fish till midnight.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_catch_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=good_catch world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say That was a catch the other day. The smokehouses are still full. | They'll be talking of that catch all season.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

## Blight in the orchards.

rule e8t_ev_blight
when concept=talk.event world.event=orchard_blight world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say Blight in the orchards, they say. Black spots on every apple. | No cider this year, if the blight keeps on.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_blight_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=orchard_blight world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say The orchards had the blight. They've burnt the worst of the trees. | The blight's done its worst. We'll see what's left come picking.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

## The festival's buying ahead.

rule e8t_ev_festival_buying
when concept=talk.event world.event=festival_buying world.event_when=soon|now
cooldown 1d
say The inns are buying ahead for the festival. | Every kitchen's stocking up for the festival.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_festival_ale
when concept=talk.event world.event=festival_buying world.event_when=soon|now world.ale_price=up
cooldown 1d
say Ale's dear already, with the festival coming. | The inns have bought the ale up for the festival. Dear now.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_festival_keeper
when concept=talk.event world.event=festival_buying world.event_when=soon|now self.job=innkeeper|cook|brewer
cooldown 1d
say I've ordered more ale than I've room for. Festival's worth it. | My cellar's full to the stairs.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

## A lame ox holding a farm's cart.

rule e8t_ev_lame_ox
when concept=talk.event world.event=lame_ox world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say No farm cart this morning. Some business with an ox. | It's all talk of #world.event_words# at the stalls. Small thing, but they feel it.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_lame_ox_carter
when concept=talk.event world.event=lame_ox world.event_when=now|past self.job=carter|farmer|herder
cooldown 1d
say Poor beast. You don't drive an ox on a bad leg, whatever the market wants. | Better a day late than an ox lost.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_lame_ox_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=lame_ox world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say The farm cart's back, after that business with the ox. | They had another ox in the shafts by morning.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

## A ship's rich cargo.

rule e8t_ev_cargo_soon
when concept=talk.event world.event=rich_cargo world.event_when=soon
cooldown 1d
say The Wharf's all talk of #world.event_words#. | They say silk and spices are coming. #world.event_words.capitalize#.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_cargo_now
when concept=talk.event world.event=rich_cargo world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say The Heights are all down at the Wharf. #world.event_words.capitalize#. | I've never seen so much silk in one place.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_cargo_spices
when concept=talk.event world.event=rich_cargo world.event_when=now world.spices_price=down
cooldown 1d
say Spices cheap at the Wharf, for once. | You can smell the spices from the square. Cheap, too.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_cargo_rich
when concept=talk.event world.event=rich_cargo world.event_when=soon|now self.wealth=rich
cooldown 1d
say I've sent the steward down for silk. Before the Heights take it all. | One waits for a ship like that all year.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_cargo_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=rich_cargo world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say The silk's all gone up the hill, after that cargo. | Half the Heights are wearing that cargo now.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

## A ship lost.

rule e8t_ev_lost
when concept=talk.event world.event=lost_ship
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say #world.event_words.capitalize#. All her cargo, gone. | They're saying it was #world.event_words#. The Wharf's gone quiet. | #world.event_words.capitalize#. The Bright One keep them.
remember pair: ev=loss 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_lost_wharf
when concept=talk.event world.event=lost_ship self.quarter=wharf|docks
cooldown 1d
priority 2
say I knew her crew. Some of them, anyway. | The sea takes what it likes. It took her.
remember pair: ev=loss 2m
then other: event.answer

## The mill wheel stopped.

rule e8t_ev_mill
when concept=talk.event world.event=mill_stopped world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say The mill wheel's stopped for mending. | No flour from the mill this week. The bakers are scraping.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_mill_bread
when concept=talk.event world.event=mill_stopped world.event_when=now world.bread_price=up
cooldown 1d
say Bread's dearer with the mill wheel stopped. | They're mending the mill wheel, and bread's dear till it turns.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_mill_baker
when concept=talk.event world.event=mill_stopped world.event_when=now self.job=baker
cooldown 1d
say No flour, no bread. I'm baking what I had put by. | I'll be glad to hear that wheel turn again.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_mill_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=mill_stopped world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say The mill wheel's turning again. You can hear it from the bridge. | They mended the mill. The bakers are back at it.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

## The drovers in.

rule e8t_ev_drovers
when concept=talk.event world.event=drovers_in world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say The drovers are in. You can hear the herds from the square. | Drovers in, and the whole yard smells of it.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_drovers_meat
when concept=talk.event world.event=drovers_in world.event_when=now world.mutton_price=down
cooldown 1d
say Mutton tonight. The drovers are in and it's cheap. | Cheap mutton, with the drovers in.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_drovers_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=drovers_in world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say The drovers have moved on. The yard's quiet again. | The tanners are still busy with what the drovers left.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

## The salt pans flooded.

rule e8t_ev_salt
when concept=talk.event world.event=salt_short world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say The salt pans are flooded, they say. | No salt to be had, with the pans under water.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_salt_winter
when concept=talk.event world.event=salt_short world.event_when=now here.season=autumn|winter
cooldown 1d
say What's a winter without salt? Ask me in a month. | The pans flooded, and the curing season on us.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_salt_fisher
when concept=talk.event world.event=salt_short world.event_when=now self.job=fisher|cook
cooldown 1d
say How am I to cure fish with no salt? | I'll smoke what I can't salt.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_salt_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=salt_short world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say The salt pans are drying out, they say. | The salt's back on the stalls, after the flood.
remember pair: ev=bad 2m
then other: event.answer

## A brewing too many.

rule e8t_ev_brew
when concept=talk.event world.event=brewers_glut world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
say The brewers have brewed too much. Barrels everywhere. | The brewers can't shift it all. I'll do my bit to help.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_brew_ale
when concept=talk.event world.event=brewers_glut world.event_when=now world.ale_price=down
cooldown 1d
say Ale's cheap! The brewers made too much. | Cheap ale this week. The brewers can't shift it.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_brew_brewer
when concept=talk.event world.event=brewers_glut world.event_when=now|past self.job=brewer
cooldown 1d
say Never brew in a hurry. I've learnt that twice now. | If you've a thirst, come and see me.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_brew_past
when concept=talk.event world.event=brewers_glut world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
say The brewers sold the last of their glut. Shame. | That was a week for ale, the brewers' glut.
remember pair: ev=good 2m
then other: event.answer

## Any other (a host's kinds), in its own words.

rule e8t_ev_any_now
when concept=talk.event world.event_when=now
cooldown 1d
priority -1
say Have you heard? #world.event_words.capitalize#. | It's all talk of #world.event_words# at the market today.
remember pair: ev=news 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_any_soon
when concept=talk.event world.event_when=soon
cooldown 1d
priority -1
say There's a notice up: #world.event_words#, in a day or two. | They're crying #world.event_words# in the square.
remember pair: ev=news 2m
then other: event.answer

rule e8t_ev_any_past
when concept=talk.event world.event_when=past
cooldown 1d
priority -1
say That business is over now: #world.event_words#. | Folk are still talking of it. #world.event_words.capitalize#.
remember pair: ev=news 2m
then other: event.answer

## Answers and the close

rule e8t_ev_ans_good
when concept=event.answer pair.mem.ev=good
say So I heard. Good for someone. | Well, that's something.

rule e8t_ev_ans_good_poor
when concept=event.answer pair.mem.ev=good self.wealth=poor|destitute
say Not that it'll reach me. | Good for those who can buy.

rule e8t_ev_ans_bad
when concept=event.answer pair.mem.ev=bad
say #oath#. That's hard news. | I'd heard. Bad business. | Let's hope it's put right soon.
then other: event.close

rule e8t_ev_ans_bad_poor
when concept=event.answer pair.mem.ev=bad self.wealth=poor|destitute
say And it's always us who feel it first. | Just what we needed.
then other: event.close

rule e8t_ev_ans_bad_rich
when concept=event.answer pair.mem.ev=bad self.wealth=rich
say How inconvenient. | Dreadful. Was anyone hurt?
then other: event.close

rule e8t_ev_ans_loss
when concept=event.answer pair.mem.ev=loss
say The Bright One keep them. | Terrible news. Terrible. | Were there families waiting for her?

rule e8t_ev_ans_news
when concept=event.answer pair.mem.ev=news
say So they say. | Is it now? Well. | I saw the notice.

rule e8t_ev_close
when concept=event.close pair.mem.ev=bad
say It'll mend. These things do. | Aye. We'll get by.
